  "implementation": [
    "One existing worktree metadata document, version 2 with explicit migration of prior version 1; no operation/event ledger. Archive retains exact original/retained paths, created provenance, Git/common-directory identities, index hash and bounded material receipt.",
    "Prepare acquires worktree and global maintenance admission, compares both saved-input raw hashes, sets a SQLite connection-local query-only seal and waits for exact related idle ACP connections to finish before returning prepared. Alias/subdirectory cwd is resolved; active or unresolved connection ownership blocks movement.",
    "Only dedicated worktree CAS can temporarily write under the same SQLite mutex. Permanent clear_all read-only protection is never undone. SQL error/unwind restores the seal; final explicit release failure produces storageUnknown with ended directory work, retained paths and continued write rejection.",
    "Blocking Git, file reads and text exports retain their actual admission after the UI/IPC waiter disappears. Git child ownership also reaps the child and waits for its process group during unwinding before maintenance admission is released.",
    "Official same-filesystem git worktree move preserves dirty, staged, untracked and ignored files. Exact identities, root material and index are checked before/after. No force/remove/clean/stash/prune/repair, no automatic retry or rollback. Archive cannot be used as an active location or forgotten; explicit restore is required.",
    "Original conversation cwd is unchanged. Both original and retained paths participate in unsent-work checks; missing draft owners never inherit the current new-draft directory. Known unrelated saved work remains allowed.",
    "Cold records become unknown and inactive in this instance; recheck does not infer completion from a path alone and preserves unknown archive metadata after acknowledgment or a new current intent."
  ],
